# The commit of ../beamtimehero_cli this repo is pinned to.
#
# The toolbelt is an editable install (`-e ../beamtimehero_cli`), so
# `import beamtimehero_cli` resolves into that sibling checkout's working
# tree: whatever is checked out there is what autonomy runs, with no
# reinstall and no diff on this side. Unpinned, a `git pull` in another
# repo changes this one's behaviour and the commit that explains a
# breakage lives somewhere else entirely.
#
# MANUALLY ADVANCED. To bump: move the sibling checkout to the new commit,
# run `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`, and only then write the SHA
# here. Keep it in step with chemcat's BEAMTIMEHERO_CLI_REF (its
# .github/workflows/ci.yaml and build-push.yaml) — both repos consume the
# same toolbelt, and drift between the two pins is the thing a pin exists
# to catch.
#
# Verified by scripts/check_cli_pin.py at start-up and by
# tests/test_cli_pin.py. Override for one run with BEAMTIMEHERO_CLI_REF,
# which takes any ref: BEAMTIMEHERO_CLI_REF=HEAD accepts whatever is
# checked out, which is what you want while developing upstream.
#
# 2026-09-13: daad45c, the same commit chemcat pins. At or above 0.5.0,
# which adds agent_surface — scripts/beamtimehero and agent_roles.py both
# import it, so an older pin does not start.
daad45c3c7109c5ef379d3ff468e80ef4469fb91
